    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d630">

                <pb facs="0790" n="666" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg666"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.51/185: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-10-24T09:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 24,
                                1921—9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 25—9:55
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>129. President Acosta last night informed me Royal Bank of Canada volunteers to
                    advance large loan to Government of Costa Rica and to undertake consolidation of
                    foreign and internal debts of the Republic. He conveyed to me the impression
                    that Huete’s<anchor n="22" xml:id="d630-f1"/> visit to the United States had
                    been unsatisfactory and that British proposal was found very interesting.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
